    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0290" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13096: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-22T21:00:00+08:00">May 22, 1935—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 22—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>210. Following telegram has been received from the Consul General at Mukden:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“May 22, 3 p.m. Premier Cheng<anchor n="53" xml:id="d130-f1"/> yesterday
                            suddenly resigned his office and a new cabinet was installed headed by
                            Chang Ching-hui<anchor n="54" xml:id="d130-f2"/> and including several
                            new appointees in replacement of former members. Political significance
                            if any is not yet apparent. A full mail report is in preparation.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d130-f1" n="53" xml:id="d130-f1-content">
                <p>Cheng Hsiao-hsu, “Manchoukuo” Prime Minister since March 1932.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d130-f2" n="54" xml:id="d130-f2-content">
                <p>Hitherto “Manchoukuo” Minister of Defense.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
